   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "The graph of the continuous function f shown consists of four line segments and a semicircle, for \\( 0 \\le t \\le 12 \\). Let \\( g(x) = \\int_{4}^{x} f(t)\\,dt \\). Find the exact value of \\( g(12) \\).",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Add",
         -8,
         [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "Pi"
         ]
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "\\( g(12) \\) is the signed area between the graph of f and the t-axis from t = 4 to t = 12.",
         "rule_named": "accumulation function as signed area"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "From t = 4 to t = 8 the graph is made of line segments, with signed areas \\( -5, -3 \\), totalling \\( -8 \\).",
         "mathjson": -8,
         "rule_named": "area of a trapezoid, negative below the axis"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "On [8, 12] the semicircle has area \\( \\tfrac{1}{2}\\pi (2)^2 = 2\\pi \\), counted as \\( 2 \\pi \\) because it lies above the axis.",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "Pi"
         ],
         "rule_named": "area of a semicircle"
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "So \\( g(12) = -8 + 2 \\pi \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Add",
            -8,
            [
               "Multiply",
               2,
               "Pi"
            ]
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99069",
         "rule_named": "additivity over adjacent intervals"
      }
   ],
